SONICLINE's build of OpenFOAM's rhoCentralFoam for slip walls (GPL-3.0-or-later,
as OpenFOAM). Nothing of OpenFOAM is kept here: the installed solver's source
($FOAM_SOLVERS/compressible/rhoCentralFoam) is copied at build time and
foam/extensions/__init__.py (PATCHES) applies one change, checked against its
anchor: the viscous work sigmaDotU carries no flux across a wall. With
velocity slip a wall face holds tau & U_slip, which rhoCentralFoam's energy
equation would otherwise take out of the gas as work on the wall (SONICLINE
DESIGN.md findings 73 and 76). With no slip U = 0 there and nothing changes.
